Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 10/04/2023]
1. Strengths from Graff et al. 1990; values agree with Sargood 1982 (Tab. 1). These values do not agree with Riihonen et al. 1979. Strength not measured by Graff et
   al., but listed in Endt 1990, have been renormalized using the Ecm = 358 keV resonance.
2. Partial widths are determined assuming Gp >> Gg.
3. For broad resonances at Ecm = 1595, 2011, and 2779 keV, the main gamma-ray decay proceeds to the ground state, see Graff et al. 1990.
4. Direct capture S factor estimated using C2S compiled in Tab. 29.22 in Endt 1990, including Vernotte et al. 1994; our adopted C2S value for the ground state 
   transition (0.55) is significantly higher than the C2S values of Graff et al. 1990 (0.36) and Terrasi et al. 1979 (0.36) that were obtained from fitting the
   28Si(p,g)29P excitation function.
5. Subthreshold states are negligible, provide an S factor at low energies of < 1e-2 keVb.
